WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Nusumareta kako wo

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
Sagashitsuzukete

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Ore wa samayou

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
Mishiranu machi wo

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Honou no nioi shimitsuite

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Museru

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Sayonara wa itta hazu da

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
Wakareta hazu sa

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
Jigoku wo mireba

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
Kokoro ga kawaku

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Tatakai wa akita no sa

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
Sadame to areba

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Kokoro wo kimeru

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Sottoshite oite kure

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Ashita ni

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Aa tsunagaru kyou gurai

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:42.830
What are you going to do, Chirico?!

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:44.170
Destroy it!

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.880
It's sending reinforcements!

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.380
Where are you going?!

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:35.630
Phantasm

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.210
Ship of unknown origin has violated our space.

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.130
Proceeding to investigate.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:18.290
Headquarters, the unidentified ship is not
answering our orders to stop. We are now...

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.380
This is the communications log tape from them?

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:24.210
Yes, sir. Two heavy cruisers were in pursuit of it.

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:28.540
This tape is from one of our patrols
on the Gilgamesh border.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:31.250
It occurred yesterday
at 13:00 hours, Balarant time.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.880
Headquarters, we are now engaging the ship.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:36.040
Enemy has launched one AT.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:40.000
Our forces consist of two Meez-class
guard ships and twenty ATs.

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:42.290
Just one AT?

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:44.250
What's the extent of their forces?

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:45.540
Unknown.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:50.330
But that one AT took out both
Meez-class ships and all twenty ATs.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:55.960
Headquarters! We've intercepted
a communication from the enemy pilot!

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.540
I can't break off the attack now!

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:03.920
You know what'll happen if they stop us
and find there's a PS onboard!

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:14.290
...and find there's a PS onboard!

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.630
He said PS...

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:18.330
A Perfect Soldier?!

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:22.460
Unknown at this time. I'm sorry, sir.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.710
We've only picked up this instance
of the term "PS" here.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:29.290
After that, they continued their pursuit of him.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:33.000
You're saying one AT destroyed all of them?

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:33.710
Yes, sir.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:37.880
According to the reports
Intelligence Division's sent me,

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:42.250
the Gilgamesh never completed
a Perfect Soldier.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:43.380
Do you think...?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.710
It's impossible.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:47.250
Intelligence's reports are true.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.790
We can't take this tape as
proof of the existence of a PS.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:54.500
And that ship's origin
still hasn't been established.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:58.290
But for one AT to have beaten all of them...

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.290
Only a PS could have done that!

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:03.210
Sir, we can't draw any conclusions.

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:05.750
We don't know where that ship came from

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:08.630
and it would be premature
to assume it's from the Gilgamesh.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:11.330
And we still have no proof PSs actually exist.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:14.210
Where is that ship headed?

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.250
It doesn't appear to be
returning to Gilgamesh space.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:22.960
Whatever the cost, we have to stop them
and learn for certain if a PS is on that ship!

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:26.500
Is that clear?! The mission will be to verify that fact.

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:30.750
Even if we're wrong,
I don't want that ship to be destroyed!

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.710
So, is this the report from our scout ship?

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:56.580
Yes, sir. A warship, origin unknown,

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:01.380
violated Balarant space and
engaged two of their patrol ships.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:05.540
It destroyed them and continued on
deeper into their territory.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:06.880
Where is it headed?

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:08.710
Unknown, sir.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:10.000
Have you identified the ship?

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.000
We've investigated all of our forces
and still can't match it.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.710
It's a Ghel-class ship, though.

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:16.330
A cruiser, eh?

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:17.920
Continue the investigation.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:18.750
Yes, sir!

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:27.040
Get me the data on the results of
the Kummen civil war.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:27.920
Yes, sir.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:37.040
Specifically, see if the bodies of
Chirico and the Prototype

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:40.880
were found among the dead
after the battle at Kanjelman's palace.

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:41.710
Yes, sir.

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.880
I doubt you will, but I want to make sure.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.540
We've had to classify every report
about those two.

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:54.710
Those two names don't show up, sir.

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:59.420
Next, I want to see the radar log
from the mission command ship.

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:00.670
Time index?

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:02.750
Around the end of the operation.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:06.500
You should find an unidentified aircraft
leaving the mission area.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:22.540
That's it. Analyze.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:23.330
Yes, sir!

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:32.130
Looks like a high-speed fighter,
probably exo-atmospheric.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:34.380
It's not a standard model.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:36.920
Now, cross reference this data

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:41.130
with the surveillance satellite computer records
for that day, same area and time index.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.420
What the...?

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:58.830
The record shows two unidentified aircraft
200 km over Kummen on that day and time.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:02.420
One of them was extremely large.

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:05.000
I see. That's how it happened...

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:08.830
Rochina here.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:11.500
We've received a secret transmission
from Bluebird.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:13.000
Bluebird?

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.960
He's undercover in Balarant territory, isn't he?

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:18.040
Their army has been making
very strange movements.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:19.040
How so?

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:21.000
They've scrambled a rapid response team.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:24.830
Three small cruisers, in pursuit of something.

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:25.540
When?

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:28.040
116 hours ago, Balarant time.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:31.710
116 hours ago...

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:35.040
They must be after that ship
that violated their space!

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:41.170
Only one thing would put them in such a sweat
to expend that much effort to capture it.

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:42.210
And that would be...!

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:51.170
You called me, sir?

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:53.830
I actually wanted to discuss
something with you as well.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:54.880
Have a seat.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:02.500
Captain, you know what sort of a person I am.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:06.080
You know I like things straight and to the point.

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:07.920
Of course, sir.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:10.500
Glad to hear it.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.540
I wouldn't want this to be taken the wrong way.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.830
Your point being, sir...?

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:17.880
You're off the case.

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.130
I'm what...?

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:22.250
Captain, how long did you think
I'd leave you in charge of the team

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:24.000
investigating Chirico and the Prototype?

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:27.710
I see. I suppose you're trying to tell me
that I've been taking too long

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:30.580
and not showing acceptable results?

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.540
I'm afraid so.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:35.540
People are starting to say we've wasted
too much time and resources.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:42.290
I think allowing the whims of politicians to dictate
policy will just lead to more trouble for us.

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:44.540
Watch your mouth, Captain!

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:49.130
I will not tolerate insubordination in my ranks!

00:11:49.130 --> 00:11:50.790
Very well, General.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:55.540
I'll step aside, as you wish.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:59.630
I'll help you to achieve your petty ambitions.

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:03.040
I was already starting to feel that the
only thing keeping me from getting Chirico

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:04.880
was the Gilgamesh system itself.

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:05.920
Excuse me.

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:08.630
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.630
Nothing...

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:13.710
Just that it's time for you and me to part ways.

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:14.750
Wait!

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.420
Captain, what was it you wanted
to talk to me about?

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:22.750
I wanted to send a covert team
into Balarant territory.

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:31.290
A warship of unknown origin has
violated Balarant space and attacked them.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:33.830
I have a feeling about that ship.

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:36.830
The enemy's already scrambled
a pursuit team to go after it.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.880
And you think Chirico and
the Prototype are on it?!

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:40.290
Who can say?

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.960
These are just the ramblings of a useless officer.

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:45.710
I imagine they're meaningless
to a great man like yourself.

00:12:45.710 --> 00:12:47.580
Well, sir... Take care.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.630
Get me the chief of Intelligence Division!

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:21.000
Chirico?! Where are you, Chirico?!

00:13:31.130 --> 00:13:32.130
Chirico!

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.420
Chirico...

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.210
Chirico...

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:07.040
Come on, let's go back to our room.

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:08.460
Make it stop...

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:10.380
Please, make the video stop.

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:12.500
Your fever still hasn't gone down.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:14.290
At least make the sound stop.

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.040
Come on, Chirico.

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:29.580
What's wrong, Chirico?!
What are you going to do?

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:32.130
Escape from this ship.

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:34.960
You can't. Not in your condition.

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:38.080
Besides, where would you go
if you left this ship?

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:40.580
Chirico...

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:51.330
Chirico!

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:55.380
Chirico...

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:37.250
What are you doing, Chirico?

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:39.080
Shoot it! I'm going to shoot it!

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:41.080
Stop it, Chirico! Calm down!

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:43.290
That screen's linked to our sensor system!

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:44.750
I'm going to shoot it!

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.210
I have to shoot! I have to shoot!

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:49.130
Chirico! Stop it, Chirico!

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:51.960
Calm down, Chirico! Just calm down!

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:00.000
Have to... shoot...

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:04.420
Forgive me, Chirico.

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:48.040
He was once a Red Shoulder.

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:54.210
But so what?

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:56.710
That has nothing to do with us now.

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:50.250
Chirico!

00:19:07.130 --> 00:19:09.130
Chirico, let's go back.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.080
Chirico...

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:14.960
Who are you?

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.960
What do you want with me?

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:23.000
What are you talking about?

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:26.250
Don't you hear it? Somebody's calling to me.

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:28.750
What do you mean? I don't hear anyone, Chirico.

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:32.460
Who are you?! What do you want with me?!

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:38.500
You want me...

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:41.580
You want me to join the rest of your companions?

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:44.880
Fine. Lead the way.

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:47.960
I'll find some way to come to you.

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:50.630
To where you all are.

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:53.290
Come on, take me!

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.420
I'll let you do what you like to me.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:19:59.170
I recognize you.

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:01.920
You're all the people I've ever killed.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:06.460
Come on, you can do whatever you want to me!

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:11.460
I don't care anymore, and I won't run away.

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:14.420
I won't run away!

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:17.580
Come on, take me to where you are!

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:20.000
Take me! Take me!

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:23.080
Chirico!

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:29.130
Chirico, snap out of it!

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:32.540
Chirico...

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:38.130
The enemy!

00:21:01.670 --> 00:21:04.920
Just wait here for me, Chirico.

00:22:13.710 --> 00:22:16.580
Fyana, why are you fighting?

00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:19.040
To protect yourself?

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:23.420
To protect me, someone who despises himself?

00:22:26.670 --> 00:22:29.290
I've been a thoughtless, miserable fool.

00:22:30.170 --> 00:22:32.960
Why have I been fighting until now?

00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:35.130
Why do I go on fighting?

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:41.540
Fyana had begun to finally pry open my heart
and I'd slammed it shut again.

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:48.670
And once more, almost unconsciously
my heart sought comfort in battle.

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:56.250 --> 00:23:00.710
The endless darkness exists
because of the brilliant stars within it.

00:23:00.830 --> 00:23:04.000
Today exists only because there is a tomorrow.

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:07.330
Heaven lies next door to this Hell.

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:10.670
It's clear to see from here. Clear to see.

00:23:11.040 --> 00:23:13.830
But that promised land is forbidden territory.

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:17.210
Next time, "Nonaggression Zone"

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:21.580
But, perhaps, today only exists
because there was a yesterday.

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:24.290
Nonaggression Zone

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Samishii toki mo

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Kanashii toki mo

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
Itsumo anata ga me ni ukabu

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Hitori no toki mo

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Aitai toki mo

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
Itsumo anata wa mune no naka

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
Tooku hanarete itemo

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
Tatoe wakarete itemo

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
Kono yo no hikari to tomo ni mabushiku

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Ano hi no anata ga...
